# Child agent stack access

Spawned subagents may **not** inherit always-on rules. Give them stack access explicitly.

## When spawning Task / any subagent

1. Prefer `~/.cursor/agents/*` agents (they embed STACK).
2. Paste the STACK block from skill `agent-stack` → `references/STACK.md` into the child prompt (dev-pipeline templates already include it).
3. For built-in `explore` / `generalPurpose`, always paste STACK.

## Stack tools children must use

Serena · rtk · explorer · caveman · Ponytail · token-saviour · coding-standards · change-handoff (when documenting)

Do not assume parent caveman/Ponytail/token-saviour rules alone cover children.

When the parent sets `CAVEMAN_OVERRIDE: off` (dev-pipeline stages 1–2 approval artifacts), that overrides STACK prose for that artifact only.
